  "problem": "Find the equation of the osculating plane (in parametric form) for the curve $r(t)$ at the point where $t=0$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t)=t\\,i+{t}^{2}\\,j+{t}^{3}\\,k,\\,T(0)=i,\\,N(0)=j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively.",
